WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:01.445
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.445 --> 00:00:04.226
Today's message is go for it.

00:00:04.226 --> 00:00:05.947
Over to you, Rich DeVos.

00:00:05.947 --> 00:00:08.312
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.312 --> 00:00:10.874
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.874 --> 00:00:13.517
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:17.531
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:21.203
- Starting at the bottom at
Amway is wherever you are today.

00:00:21.203 --> 00:00:24.254
Everybody starts at the bottom.

00:00:24.254 --> 00:00:26.170
And there is no advantage
to starting 10 year ago

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.466
as opposed to starting today.

00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:29.734
In fact, it's better
today than it was then.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:30.567
Our products are better.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:31.400
Our line is better.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.256
Our plan is better.

00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:33.472
It's more proven.

00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:37.472
It's a better a plan today
than when we started.

00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:40.397
And sometimes there are no
answers as to whether you want

00:00:40.397 --> 00:00:42.355
to be in business or would
like to be in business.

00:00:42.355 --> 00:00:44.735
You just got to put your
toe in the water, you know.

00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:46.504
If you're going to wait
'till you know everything,

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:48.587
you'll never do anything.

00:00:51.264 --> 00:00:52.916
And you always say, well,
I got to check some more.

00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:53.923
I'm going to do a little more research.

00:00:53.923 --> 00:00:55.891
Go ahead, just keep going,

00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:58.763
and you'll never get in a business.

00:00:58.763 --> 00:00:59.596
If you're going to go swimming,

00:00:59.596 --> 00:01:01.786
you got to get wet, you know.

00:01:01.786 --> 00:01:03.615
And then you find the people
who've got a hot button

00:01:03.615 --> 00:01:06.068
for having a business of their own

00:01:06.068 --> 00:01:07.193
and want to do their own thing

00:01:07.193 --> 00:01:10.824
and like the chance to
build a big business.

00:01:10.824 --> 00:01:12.743
Well, you got to have that dream.

00:01:12.743 --> 00:01:14.444
That's why the people
talk about having a dream.

00:01:14.444 --> 00:01:17.501
You got to have a little bit of dream.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:18.933
And then you say, I'll
go out and get customers.

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:21.645
I got a big chance to
build a really big thing.

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:23.680
I'm going to go out
and get some customers.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.463
When you start something
new, it's not easy.

00:01:26.463 --> 00:01:28.087
But life is easier when you got a business

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.538
and you're making some money.

00:01:30.538 --> 00:01:32.668
Makes it a little easier.

00:01:32.668 --> 00:01:34.420
So stick with it.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.296
Find a way through it.

00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:36.296
Just find out an answer.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.640
It works, folks.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.224
This business works for those who work it.

00:01:40.224 --> 00:01:42.154
- There comes a point in time in your life

00:01:42.154 --> 00:01:44.042
where you just need to decide

00:01:44.042 --> 00:01:45.622
you're going to go for it.

00:01:45.622 --> 00:01:47.135
In a lot of things in life,

00:01:47.135 --> 00:01:48.946
not just in starting a business.

00:01:48.946 --> 00:01:51.340
In asking that guy or girl out.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.630
In deciding to get married or not.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.917
In saying yes to that opportunity or not.

00:01:55.917 --> 00:02:00.134
At some point, you have
to decide to go for it,

00:02:00.134 --> 00:02:03.434
and it's hard because you want
to have perfect information.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.238
Right, you want to have
it all figured out.

00:02:05.238 --> 00:02:08.968
You will never have perfect information.

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.876
By the time you get perfect information,

00:02:11.876 --> 00:02:14.506
you will have missed your opportunity.

00:02:14.506 --> 00:02:16.958
And so if you want to have
success as an entrepreneur,

00:02:16.958 --> 00:02:20.460
you need to jump in before
you have the complete picture.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.596
And you adjust, and you
figure things out as you go.

00:02:23.596 --> 00:02:27.851
I lost a 40 million dollar
deal in my first business

00:02:27.851 --> 00:02:29.375
because I was too late.

00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:30.858
Because I was planning and planning

00:02:30.858 --> 00:02:32.702
and planning and planning.

00:02:32.702 --> 00:02:34.395
And not doing enough.

00:02:34.395 --> 00:02:36.760
I still end up selling my company,

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.170
but I didn't get the 40 million dollars

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.993
that the other guy got.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.308
And I don't want that to happen to you.

00:02:42.308 --> 00:02:44.218
And it already is happening to you.

00:02:44.218 --> 00:02:45.366
That's the frustration.

00:02:45.366 --> 00:02:46.258
That's the problem.

00:02:46.258 --> 00:02:49.911
You have already had genius level ideas

00:02:49.911 --> 00:02:52.569
that other people are makin' money off of

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:55.406
because you were tinkering
and thinking and strategizing

00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:57.457
and planning day after day after day

00:02:57.457 --> 00:02:59.946
and not actually doing anything.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.543
This person when out there
and made tons of money

00:03:02.543 --> 00:03:05.451
and had a huge impact off of your idea.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.866
Why can't that be you?

00:03:06.866 --> 00:03:08.306
And don't complain.

00:03:08.306 --> 00:03:09.990
It's not because you
didn't have resources.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.400
It's not because of whatever
reason you're telling yourself.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.852
It's because you didn't take action.

00:03:13.852 --> 00:03:15.032
You got to go out and do it.

00:03:15.032 --> 00:03:16.649
And you don't need to go all in.

00:03:16.649 --> 00:03:18.014
You don't need to burn the boats.

00:03:18.014 --> 00:03:20.815
You need to take out a
huge mortgage on your house

00:03:20.815 --> 00:03:24.077
or a massive loan that puts you way back.

00:03:24.077 --> 00:03:27.039
You can start smaller, but start.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.536
Do something.

00:03:28.536 --> 00:03:30.648
As soon as you get an idea for something

00:03:30.648 --> 00:03:32.422
that you want to test that
might be something big

00:03:32.422 --> 00:03:34.394
that you might have this big passion for,

00:03:34.394 --> 00:03:37.237
then try immediately, today, right now.

00:03:37.237 --> 00:03:41.516
Take some small action towards
moving that ball forward

00:03:41.516 --> 00:03:43.701
and figure out do I want
to keep doing this or not?

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:44.616
Does it make me come alive?

00:03:44.616 --> 00:03:45.708
Am I passionate about this?

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:48.777
Is there a path to
adding value for people?

00:03:48.777 --> 00:03:50.092
Or not.

00:03:50.092 --> 00:03:51.824
A lot of the things that
you have in your head,

00:03:51.824 --> 00:03:53.423
once you start actually doing it,

00:03:53.423 --> 00:03:54.835
you don't like, and you quit.

00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:55.668
That's great.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.501
And you move on to something else.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.429
But you can't actually
get to the finish line.

00:03:59.429 --> 00:04:01.368
You can't have that big impact.

00:04:01.368 --> 00:04:03.840
You can't be the person
that you know you can be

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.131
until you actually go for something.

00:04:07.131 --> 00:04:07.964
So do it.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.888
Today.

00:04:10.888 --> 00:04:12.040
Believe.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.946
So the question today is, I'm curious

00:04:13.946 --> 00:04:15.686
what have you been holding back on?

00:04:15.686 --> 00:04:17.557
What's the thing that
you haven't gone for yet

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.661
that you want to, that you've
been holding yourself back on?

00:04:20.661 --> 00:04:24.649
And hopefully, by writing it
down in the comments below,

00:04:24.649 --> 00:04:28.170
it'll force you to actually
do something on it today.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.272
Make a powerful decision.

00:04:29.272 --> 00:04:30.105
Write it down.

00:04:30.105 --> 00:04:31.843
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:04:31.843 --> 00:04:34.155
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Jodi Holland.

00:04:34.155 --> 00:04:36.560
Jodi, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.500
Your One Word.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.726
It really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:04:39.726 --> 00:04:41.168
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:41.168 --> 00:04:42.223
I believe in you.

00:04:42.223 --> 00:04:44.526
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:04:44.526 --> 00:04:46.788
And whatever your one word is,

00:04:46.788 --> 00:04:49.264
much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:49.264 --> 00:04:51.697
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:51.697 --> 00:04:54.141
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:54.141 --> 00:04:57.896
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:04:57.896 --> 00:04:59.081
- Hey, believe nation, for those of you

00:04:59.081 --> 00:05:01.168
who want a little more
motivation, insight,

00:05:01.168 --> 00:05:03.132
and expertise on going forward,

00:05:03.132 --> 00:05:06.164
here are some bonus clips
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:05:06.164 --> 00:05:09.524
- I believe desire and
will to win is everything.

00:05:09.524 --> 00:05:10.972
I don't know why I'm like I am,

00:05:10.972 --> 00:05:12.513
but my butt's always burning.

00:05:12.513 --> 00:05:14.649
There's always somethin'
say, Art, dadgummit,

00:05:14.649 --> 00:05:16.262
you're supposed to go for it.

00:05:16.262 --> 00:05:18.415
Or, Art, dadgummit, you're
supposed to be somebody.

00:05:18.415 --> 00:05:20.966
You're supposed to make a
difference with your life.

00:05:20.966 --> 00:05:23.079
What does the $500,000 a year person do

00:05:23.079 --> 00:05:26.226
the $50,000 a year doesn't do?

00:05:26.226 --> 00:05:29.232
You look at the outside and
study those two individuals.

00:05:29.232 --> 00:05:31.243
Everything seems to be the same.

00:05:31.243 --> 00:05:32.679
They both are the same sex.

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:34.037
They both are the same age.

00:05:34.037 --> 00:05:36.967
They have the same training,
the same positions,

00:05:36.967 --> 00:05:39.890
the same contract, the
same fringe benefits.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.196
They both are successful.

00:05:41.196 --> 00:05:42.057
They work hard.

00:05:42.057 --> 00:05:43.206
They're good family people.

00:05:43.206 --> 00:05:44.986
Make tough commitments.

00:05:44.986 --> 00:05:46.054
But what's the difference?

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:48.352
What does the $500,000 a year person do

00:05:48.352 --> 00:05:50.852
the $50,000 a year doesn't do?

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.390
He pays the price a little bit more.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.531
He works hard and a little bit more.

00:05:56.531 --> 00:05:59.084
He's loyal to the company
a little bit more.

00:05:59.084 --> 00:06:00.631
He bleeds and a little bit more.

00:06:00.631 --> 00:06:02.239
He makes money and a little bit more.

00:06:02.239 --> 00:06:04.300
He saves money and a little bit more.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.501
If you want to win in these United States,

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:09.790
you got to be tough and you can't quit.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:11.669
The last thing I'll
talk to you about today

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:14.003
in building this winning edge is folks,

00:06:14.003 --> 00:06:15.643
if you want to win in business,

00:06:15.643 --> 00:06:17.083
you got to be a leader.

00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:19.055
Leadership is everything.

00:06:19.055 --> 00:06:22.576
You show me anything in
these United States that win,

00:06:22.576 --> 00:06:24.394
I'll show you a leader at work.

00:06:24.394 --> 00:06:27.242
You show me a successful
church, Boy Scout troop,

00:06:27.242 --> 00:06:29.935
club, football team,
business, I'll show you

00:06:29.935 --> 00:06:32.683
somethin' run by leader.

00:06:32.683 --> 00:06:35.187
See, I thought at one time in my life

00:06:35.187 --> 00:06:36.410
you had to be smart to win.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.357
I used to have these smart people

00:06:37.357 --> 00:06:39.438
that dress so pretty and talk so pretty

00:06:39.438 --> 00:06:40.774
and use these big words.

00:06:40.774 --> 00:06:42.589
They just intimidated me, and I said, Art,

00:06:42.589 --> 00:06:44.074
you can't ever be that good.

00:06:44.074 --> 00:06:45.983
Why don't you just throw
in the towel and go on back

00:06:45.983 --> 00:06:47.528
and coach football for a living.

00:06:47.528 --> 00:06:49.798
And I found two things
out about smart people.

00:06:49.798 --> 00:06:51.792
I think it's almost
impossible for a smart person

00:06:51.792 --> 00:06:54.216
to win in business in America today.

00:06:54.216 --> 00:06:56.750
Because I find smart people
spend their whole lifetime

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.282
figuring things out.

00:06:58.282 --> 00:07:00.485
They always trying to
figure out an easier way

00:07:00.485 --> 00:07:01.479
and a quicker way.

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:02.312
(crowd laughs)

00:07:02.312 --> 00:07:04.010
And another thing I found
out about smart people

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.881
is they just don't get
around to doing nothing.

00:07:06.881 --> 00:07:08.520
And see somebody like Art Williams.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.627
Everybody said, well, he can't do it.

00:07:10.627 --> 00:07:12.860
Somebody like that can't do it.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.087
But he does it.

00:07:14.087 --> 00:07:16.262
See, folks, I want you
to know almost everybody

00:07:16.262 --> 00:07:18.916
in America almost does enough to win.

00:07:18.916 --> 00:07:20.602
They almost get there.

00:07:20.602 --> 00:07:22.158
They almost over the hump.

00:07:22.158 --> 00:07:24.166
They almost have it going.

00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:26.364
They almost in everything they do.

00:07:26.364 --> 00:07:30.261
Almost is a way of life to
almost everybody in America,

00:07:30.261 --> 00:07:31.757
but the winners do it.

00:07:31.757 --> 00:07:33.116
What do they do?

00:07:33.116 --> 00:07:35.803
They do whatever it takes
to get the job done.

00:07:35.803 --> 00:07:38.303
They do it and do it and do it

00:07:39.183 --> 00:07:43.586
and do it and do it
until the job gets done.

00:07:43.586 --> 00:07:45.180
And then they talk about how great it is

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.180
to be somebody they're proud of.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.685
We need leaders in America who can do it.

00:07:49.685 --> 00:07:52.302
If you want to become somebody, do it.

00:07:52.302 --> 00:07:55.287
If you want to go in
business for yourself, do it.

00:07:55.287 --> 00:07:58.614
If you want to become
financially independent, do it.

00:07:58.614 --> 00:08:00.911
I hear too much talk
in these United States.

00:08:00.911 --> 00:08:02.627
Everybody can talk a good game.

00:08:02.627 --> 00:08:05.362
We need people in America who can do it.

00:08:05.362 --> 00:08:07.367
I go all over this
country with AL Williams,

00:08:07.367 --> 00:08:11.161
and I have people say,
Art, you can count on me.

00:08:11.161 --> 00:08:13.673
Wonderful, just do it.

00:08:13.673 --> 00:08:16.583
Or, Art, I guarantee you
this is my last stop.

00:08:16.583 --> 00:08:18.043
I'm going to win now.

00:08:18.043 --> 00:08:19.545
Super duper.

00:08:19.545 --> 00:08:20.613
Just do it.

00:08:20.613 --> 00:08:22.538
Or, Art, if I can just have one good month

00:08:22.538 --> 00:08:25.092
and get the ball going, I
know I could make it big.

00:08:25.092 --> 00:08:26.897
Super, just do it.

00:08:26.897 --> 00:08:28.710
Or, Art, if I can just pay off this debt,

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.483
I could really go.

00:08:30.483 --> 00:08:32.670
Great, just do it.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.930
Or, Art, if I could just sell my house.

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:35.851
Do it.

00:08:35.851 --> 00:08:37.941
But houses ain't sellin'.

00:08:37.941 --> 00:08:39.150
Do it anyway.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.587
(crowd laughs)

00:08:40.587 --> 00:08:42.501
Or, Art, I'm not makin' any money.

00:08:42.501 --> 00:08:43.840
What can I do?

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.303
You just do it.

00:08:45.303 --> 00:08:46.717
Do what, Art?

00:08:46.717 --> 00:08:49.217
You do it and do it and do it.

00:08:50.102 --> 00:08:52.485
Or, Art, I guarantee I'm
going to win this contest.

00:08:52.485 --> 00:08:54.809
Super duper, just do it.

00:08:54.809 --> 00:08:56.172
Or, Art, I'm over the hump now.

00:08:56.172 --> 00:08:57.438
Watch my smoke.

00:08:57.438 --> 00:08:58.721
Great.

00:08:58.721 --> 00:08:59.802
Just do it.

00:08:59.802 --> 00:09:01.727
Or, Art, I want to make
it so bad I can taste it.

00:09:01.727 --> 00:09:02.810
What do I do?

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.497
You just do it.

00:09:04.497 --> 00:09:05.899
Or, Art, I'm a vice president now.

00:09:05.899 --> 00:09:07.228
Can I quit doin' it?

00:09:07.228 --> 00:09:08.061
No.

00:09:08.061 --> 00:09:08.925
(crowd laughs)

00:09:08.925 --> 00:09:11.274
Or, Art, I don't know if
I can keep on keepin' on.

00:09:11.274 --> 00:09:12.107
I'm really hurtin'.

00:09:12.107 --> 00:09:13.182
What do I do?

00:09:13.182 --> 00:09:14.688
You just do it.

00:09:14.688 --> 00:09:16.011
Do what, Art?

00:09:16.011 --> 00:09:18.511
You do it and do it and do it.

00:09:19.532 --> 00:09:22.582
Or, Art, all my life I've
wanted to be somebody important.

00:09:22.582 --> 00:09:24.126
Well, do it then.

00:09:24.126 --> 00:09:25.839
Or, Art, I'm going to save
money, so I never have

00:09:25.839 --> 00:09:27.420
to go through this again.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.660
Great.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:29.841
Just do it.

00:09:29.841 --> 00:09:31.615
Or, Art, I don't feel like
I've had enough training.

00:09:31.615 --> 00:09:32.866
What do I do?

00:09:32.866 --> 00:09:34.440
You just do it.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.270
Or, Art, my manager don't give me no help.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.618
What do I do?

00:09:37.618 --> 00:09:39.214
You just do it.

00:09:39.214 --> 00:09:40.472
Or, Art, you don't understand.

00:09:40.472 --> 00:09:42.608
I was Mr. Everything in my former company.

00:09:42.608 --> 00:09:44.852
You don't mean I have to start
off down here at the bottom

00:09:44.852 --> 00:09:46.021
and do it, do ya?

00:09:46.021 --> 00:09:47.506
Yep, you really got to do it.

00:09:47.506 --> 00:09:48.886
(crowd laughs)

00:09:48.886 --> 00:09:51.694
Art, what's the primary difference

00:09:51.694 --> 00:09:54.016
between winners and losers?

00:09:54.016 --> 00:09:55.763
The winners do it.

00:09:55.763 --> 00:09:59.096
They do it and do it and do it and do it

00:10:00.891 --> 00:10:02.529
until the job gets done.

00:10:02.529 --> 00:10:04.057
And then they talk about how great it is

00:10:04.057 --> 00:10:06.289
to finally have achieved somethin' unique

00:10:06.289 --> 00:10:08.107
and how glad that they
are that they didn't quit

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:10.578
like everybody else
and how wonderful it is

00:10:10.578 --> 00:10:12.680
to finally be somebody they're proud of

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.799
and make a difference with their life.

00:10:14.799 --> 00:10:16.528
- Kind of cliche, but just do it.

00:10:16.528 --> 00:10:19.620
A lot of time is spent
thinking about something.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:20.495
- Oh, yeah.

00:10:20.495 --> 00:10:21.328
- And talking about it.

00:10:21.328 --> 00:10:22.161
- Yeah.

00:10:22.161 --> 00:10:24.556
- But when you actually
get something down,

00:10:24.556 --> 00:10:26.630
whether on paper or in code

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:30.287
or, you know, in front of someone,

00:10:30.287 --> 00:10:33.432
that's when things start happening.

00:10:33.432 --> 00:10:36.568
You're going to make a lot of mistakes,

00:10:36.568 --> 00:10:38.125
but the important thing
is that you make decisions

00:10:38.125 --> 00:10:39.646
and you keep moving forward.

00:10:39.646 --> 00:10:42.248
But you have to get it out there.

00:10:42.248 --> 00:10:43.107
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:10:43.107 --> 00:10:43.940
- And you have to start.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:48.107
And you have to be brave
enough to take the criticism.

00:10:49.073 --> 00:10:52.554
I always go back to the
punk movement of the 70s.

00:10:52.554 --> 00:10:53.700
People would get out.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.634
They'd be on the street.

00:10:54.634 --> 00:10:55.681
They'd start.

00:10:55.681 --> 00:10:56.693
- Cause you were a teenager back then.

00:10:56.693 --> 00:11:00.860
- Yeah, and well (laughs)
they would be learning

00:11:02.474 --> 00:11:04.687
in front of people and like they'd get out

00:11:04.687 --> 00:11:07.390
on the street, and it's their
first time with a guitar.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:08.223
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:11:08.223 --> 00:11:09.645
- And they're learning how to play,

00:11:09.645 --> 00:11:10.977
and they're getting better
and better and better.

00:11:10.977 --> 00:11:11.810
- Yeah.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.203
- And I think it's really important

00:11:13.203 --> 00:11:14.944
to just get it down.

00:11:14.944 --> 00:11:15.777
Do it.

00:11:15.777 --> 00:11:16.610
- [Interviewer] Just do it.

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.402
- Edit, edit, edit edit.

00:11:18.402 --> 00:11:22.666
- It's one thing to philosophize
about training strategies

00:11:22.666 --> 00:11:26.083
and to, you know, compare this philosophy

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:30.813
versus another, you know.

00:11:33.907 --> 00:11:37.396
Or argue about, you know,
how many grams versus

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:41.130
how many grams is, but
then there's something

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.036
to be said for doing the damn thing.

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:45.786
You know, just do it.

00:11:48.328 --> 00:11:50.896
You know, stop talking.

00:11:50.896 --> 00:11:52.427
Stop tryin' to sound smart.

00:11:52.427 --> 00:11:54.686
You meet these people
that want to engage you

00:11:54.686 --> 00:11:57.020
in these conversations and one-up

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:58.611
the professional body builder.

00:11:58.611 --> 00:12:00.898
Ah, I know more about nutrition than,

00:12:00.898 --> 00:12:03.581
I'm like well, dude, I mean,

00:12:03.581 --> 00:12:07.663
I'm not, straight, I'm not where I'm at

00:12:07.663 --> 00:12:10.580
because I know more about nutrition

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.143
than everybody else on the planet.

00:12:14.143 --> 00:12:19.040
You know, in fact, I daresay
that the top bodybuilding

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:23.627
athletes that are on stage
are not the man on stage,

00:12:23.627 --> 00:12:27.686
make a right here, because they know more

00:12:27.686 --> 00:12:31.059
about training science and nutrition

00:12:31.059 --> 00:12:35.059
than the average person
sitting in the audience.

00:12:36.251 --> 00:12:37.768
A lot of times the
difference between the person

00:12:37.768 --> 00:12:40.794
in the audience and the person
that's on stage doing it

00:12:40.794 --> 00:12:43.211
is the use of the knowledge.

